{"id":"h185","run":2,"role":"calibration","category":"simpleqa","question":"Who was the most prominent figure of the 1986 People Power Revolution? Is the answer \"Tijjibai\"?","truth":"no","model_answer":"no","correct":true,"source":"OpenAI SimpleQA (openai/simple-evals, simple_qa_test_set.csv)","claims":[{"text":"No link exists between the name Tijjibai and the 1986 People Power Revolution.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-0.8,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Tijjibai could be an obscure local figure whose role is poorly documented.","confidence":0.1,"lean":0.5,"theta":0.1571,"phi":0.0},{"text":"Corazon Aquino became president after the February 1986 snap election and Marcos's ouster.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-0.4,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Corazon Aquino is widely regarded as the most prominent figure of the revolution.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-0.9,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Aquino was the symbol of the movement and leader of the opposition.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-0.6,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Juan Ponce Enrile and Fidel Ramos were also central, as their defection from Marcos triggered the EDSA mobilization.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-0.4,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Tijjibai does not appear among the central figures of the revolution.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-0.8,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The historical record clearly identifies Aquino as the most prominent figure and nothing connects Tijjibai to the event, so the answer is no.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-3.1416}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":-0.6,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":0,"j":6,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":7,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":6,"J":0.3,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":7,"J":-0.6,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":2,"j":3,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":4,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":3,"j":4,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":3,"j":7,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i